Particles Life Time System

Simple... What if we just take the emitter.particleLifetime as the "how much time this emitter needs to wait before being destroyed".

Also we immediatly set spawn rate and spaw speed to 0 so the emitter doesn't emit more particles.

The idea is "At this point, the particles should just die at their time".

So each emitter should be put on a list of "emitters to be destroyed".

When put there, we set the amount of time to wait (the particleLifetime), spawn rate and spaw speed to 0 and initialize a counter for that emitter.

Each frame we check that list and on each one we substract timestate.deltaTime

We check if the counter is less or equal than 0 and if it is we remove that emitter from the list (by swapping with the last one).
